 ],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Internal structure",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "One die holds a PNP transistor with integrated resistors and two diodes. The internal resistor Rint is 48 kΩ typical."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Setting the current",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "With REXT open the output is typically 15 µA. A resistor between VS and REXT adds 0.617 / Rext to that, up to a 50 mA ceiling."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply voltage and current",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "How much current is available depends on the supply. Running at 70 % of the most the part can deliver, typical figures are 6 mA at 5 V, 18 mA at 12 V, 38 mA at 24 V and 60 mA at 36 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "On/off control",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Breaking the GND pin's return with a resistor-equipped transistor such as the PDTC124XU turns the output current on and off."
  }
 ],
